# Deleting files on servers

User rule of 2026-11-13. A disk-reclaim agent removed the malware-feed study's repeat-run
workspace and its off-host custody copy (after running `chattr -i` on it) during the repeat
measurement. Full rule: `AGENTS.md`, section "Deleting files on servers".

- Never delete, move or truncate any path whose name starts with `mfa-`, anything under
  `research/` or `/root/mfa-study/`, or the `mfa-*` units, timers and holder containers.
  A date in a folder name does not make it scrap.
- Never run `chattr -i` / `chattr -a`, and never change permissions or ownership to make a
  deletion work. An immutable flag means stop and ask the user.
- Disk reclaim is ask-first: report the survey, then delete only paths this session created
  or the user approved by exact path. Never brief another agent with "old MFA/test scrap".
- No `docker container|volume|image prune` on hosts with study or HISTOR sandbox services;
  holder containers keep needed images.
- No `logrotate -f` and no deleting rotated logs or `wtmp` to free space.
